      "end_mono": 356477.922259083,
      "raw_response": " F. Type 1 diabetes is not caused by food\n\nType 1 diabetes is an autoimmune disease, meaning the body's immune system mistakenly attacks and destroys the insulin-producing cells in the pancreas (beta cells). The exact causes of Type 1 diabetes are not fully understood, but it is believed that a combination of genetic and environmental factors play a role.\n\nCommon environmental triggers for Type 1 diabetes are viral infections and certain dietary factors, but eating sugar or carbohydrates is not among them. The misconception that eating sugar causes Type 1 diabetes likely arises due to the association between high blood sugar levels and symptoms of the disease, but it is the body's inability to produce insulin, not the consumption of sugar, that leads to high blood sugar levels.\n\nANSWER: F",
